  "name": "kirby",
  "notes": "Kirby validation suite: 43 games across all six legal stages. 26 are corpus games against Zelda, Ice Climbers, Game & Watch, Falco, Marth, Captain Falcon, Peach and a level-6 CPU Bowser: three 2026 Mainline Slippi Dolphin recordings by the user (the Bowser game runs through the recorded-input CPU lane and copies Fire Breath), fourteen 2023-2026 Dolphin games (greg), and nine Wii console captures from D20 Melee #1, #3 and #37 (Slippi Nintendont, offline VS scene). 17 are scripted headless Dolphin captures (tools/validation/record_kirby_copies.exs, the pinned accurate-nmsub build) in which Kirby swallows Mario, Luigi, Dr. Mario, Link, Young Link, Samus, Sheik, Ness, Pikachu, Jigglypuff, Mewtwo, Donkey Kong, Yoshi, Ganondorf, Fox or another Kirby, fires the copy on the ground and in the air, drops it by taunt, re-swallows, then loses it to hits and death; one more drives Final Cutter, Hammer and Stone around Battlefield's platforms and ledges. Together with the corpus copies (Zelda, Ice Climbers, Game & Watch, Falco, Marth, Captain Falcon, Peach, Bowser) every copy ability except Pichu and Roy is locked; those two wait for their own admissions. The second D20 #1 Falco game is classified missing-raw-cstick-asdi: its Slippi 3.15 capture records only the normalized C-stick, so a 79/80 cardinal at hitlag exit cannot be told from a clamped full deflection. Pokemon Stadium entries validate end to end against the Frozen Stadium owner (no transformation occurs in them). The suite is exact on the PPC oracle as well. Provenance and the triaged exclusions: agent_docs/validation/kirby_provenance.json.",
